    note: "Removes the shared-database hazard that cost wave 44 a fix attempt. Its own three db_required tests are among those 12 skips, which is the evidence hole it exposed; the gate_condition_change below is what closes it."
wave_44_complete:
  at: 2026-10-17T19:20:43Z
  cards: [CARD-243, CARD-222, CARD-236]
  merged: 3
  escalations: 0
  smoke_test: "SATISFIED by CARD-236's merge gate without a separate run: 7895 passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed in 784.64s, and `git diff 6b27c08 HEAD -- src/ tests/ migrations/ pyproject.toml` is empty, so main's code tree is byte-identical to the gated tree. Same reasoning as wave 43's."
  note: "3/3 merged, 0 escalations. The suite ENDED THE WAVE FASTER THAN IT STARTED -- 913s at CARD-243's gate to 784.64s at CARD-236's -- while gaining 52 tests (7843 -> 7895), because CARD-236 was a cost card. Two process defects dominated the wave and both are backlog items now: the shared nonogram_test database has no lock (db_session TRUNCATEs it per test, so concurrent cards corrupt each other -- it cost CARD-222 a whole fix attempt chasing a 48-skip regression that did not exist), and an architect amendment landing mid-card invalidated an exemption claim the card had written correctly against the pre-amendment rule."
refill_deferred_resolved:
  freed_by: "CARD-222 merged 40a93dd"
  outcome: "Never refilled, and correctly so: CARD-236 merged 20 minutes later, which completed the wave. A refill would have started a card into a wave that was about to close, and into the DB hazard above."

