    actual: 0.5d
    estimate: 0.5d
    accuracy: 0.92x
    gate: "7895 passed, 9 skipped, 0 failed in 784.64s; code tree byte-identical to the gated commit 6b27c08"
    note: "The card's PREMISE was wrong and that is the deliverable: the trio's 117s is the first execve of a newly CREATED executable under Defender real-time protection, not subprocess spawning. Solo measurement at the merge gate settled AC-1/G-3: trio 140.79s -> 13.73s (10.25x), suite 924.53s -> 784.64s (-15.1%) while gaining 22 tests. Its own projected 1.64% share measured 3.20% -- optimistic by 2x, recorded rather than replaced. Nine mutants replayed against both test sets with a no-mutant control green on BOTH sides."
refill_deferred:
  freed_by: "CARD-222 merged 40a93dd"
  slot: 1
  reason: "NOT refilled yet, deliberately. CARD-236 is at its own merge gate running a full suite, and this board's rule is that merges run sequentially and never alongside concurrent full suites. Starting a third agent now would also re-create the exact hazard that cost CARD-222 a fix attempt: conftest's db_session TRUNCATEs the shared nonogram_test before every test, so a new card's DB selections would corrupt the gate in flight. Refill once CARD-236 lands."
  eligible_when_refilled: "CARD-222's dependents whose conflict edges were only to it — CARD-206, CARD-207 (book_pdf_generator.py), CARD-208, CARD-209, CARD-215 (export/layout.py), CARD-220 (tests/**), plus CARD-223..CARD-227 and CARD-229..CARD-233 by dependency. Note CARD-227 and CARD-230 are now pre-dispatch clean (their contradictions and mis-cut ACs were settled this wave), while CARD-225 has newly inherited AC-370 as a blocking obligation."

